@event marsh_grandmother_lesson
# en: The Old Work
title [ecb5e6] = 老手艺
# en: {Your grandmother has decided the academy has taught you nothing useful, and sets out the mortar to prove it.|The mortar is out again. "Again," she says, "and this time listen to it."|You reach for the mortar before she asks. She pretends not to notice, and is pleased.} {season == "winter": Frost on the reeds outside; inside, the stove and the smell of dried meadowsweet.|The windows open on the marsh's hum; flies argue with the drying bunches.}
text [bb63bb] = {你外婆认定学院什么有用的都没教你，于是摆出研钵来证明这一点。|研钵又摆出来了。“再来，”她说，“这回好好听它的声音。”|她还没开口，你就伸手去拿研钵了。她装作没看见，心里很高兴。} {season == "winter": 外面芦苇上结着霜；屋里是炉火和晒干的绣线菊的气味。|窗子朝着沼泽的嗡鸣敞开；苍蝇在晾着的草药束间争吵。}
# en: Inside a small house on stilts above a marsh, an old woman and a young student bent over a table of drying herbs, jars and a mortar.
scene [ca74f4] = 沼泽上一座高脚屋里，一位老妇人和一个年轻学生俯身在一张摆满晾干草药、罐子和研钵的桌前。
# en: Do it her way, slowly
opt.left.label [62fe1b] = 照她的法子慢慢来
# en: {Two hours on one poultice. Your wrist aches. She tastes it, nods once, and puts it on the shelf with her own.|She makes you grind until the paste stops sounding gritty and your shoulders burn. You hadn't known paste had a sound.|You do it her way without being told, two hours bent over the mortar until your back aches. She says nothing at all, which is how you know.}
opt.left.say.1 [07780b] = {一帖膏药做了两个钟头。你的手腕酸了。她尝了尝，点了一下头，把它和她自己做的放在同一个架子上。|她让你一直磨，直到药糊不再发出沙沙声，你的肩膀火辣辣地疼。你以前不知道药糊还有声音。|你不等她说就照她的法子做，在研钵前弯腰两个钟头，直到腰都酸了。她一句话也没说，你就知道了。}
# en: Show her the academy way
opt.right.label [ab2a4d] = 给她看学院的法子
# en: {You do it in ten minutes with a charm. She sniffs it, says "It'll keep a week," and makes you do it again her way after supper.|{flag(marsh_charm_shown): You show her the charm again. She watches closer this time, and doesn't say it's wrong.|You show her the charm. She watches with her lips pressed together, then has you do it twice more.}|{flag(marsh_charm_shown): She asks you to teach her the charm. Then she tells you three things it does that the professors never mentioned.|You show her a charm. She makes you explain every word of it, then tells you its old name.}}
opt.right.say.1 [79c98d] = {你用一道咒语十分钟就做好了。她闻了闻，说“能放一个星期”，晚饭后又让你照她的法子重做一遍。|{flag(marsh_charm_shown): 你又演示了一遍那道咒语。这回她看得更仔细，没说它不对。|你给她演示那道咒语。她抿着嘴看完，又让你做了两遍。}|{flag(marsh_charm_shown): 她请你教她那道咒语。然后她告诉你它还有三种教授们从没提过的用处。|你给她演示一道咒语。她让你把每个词都解释一遍，然后告诉你它的老名字。}}

@event marsh_stilt_house_supper
# en: Supper Above the Water
title [d36aff] = 水上的晚饭
# en: {Eel pie, black bread and the marsh going quiet outside. Your grandmother wants to hear about the castle, all of it.|Supper again, and the questions again, sharper this time: who your friends are, whether they're good to you.|Supper, and this time she talks first: the year the river froze, the winter the wolves came to the edge. Then she wants your news.} {final_year: She asks what comes after, and listens to the whole answer.|Out on the water, a light drifts past the window. She shuts the shutter without comment.}
text [77de68] = {鳗鱼馅饼、黑面包，外面的沼泽渐渐安静下来。你外婆想听城堡里的事，一件不落。|又是晚饭，又是那些问题，这回问得更尖：你的朋友是谁，他们待你好不好。|晚饭时，这回是她先开口：河水结冰的那一年，狼群来到村边的那个冬天。然后她要听你的消息。} {final_year: 她问你之后有什么打算，把你的回答一字不落地听完。|窗外的水面上，一点光漂了过去。她一声不响地关上了百叶窗。}
# en: A small house on stilts at dusk, lamplight in its window, an old woman and a student eating at a table by the open shutter over dark water.
scene [1ee94d] = 黄昏时一座高脚屋，窗里亮着灯，一位老妇人和一个学生在敞开的窗板边吃饭，窗外是黑沉沉的水。
# en: Tell her everything
opt.left.label [92d56a] = 什么都告诉她
# en: {You talk until the lamp gutters and long past your bedtime. She laughs at the professor who throws chalk and goes very quiet at the duelling.|You tell her about your friends until the lamp's out. She asks two questions about each, both of them the right ones.|You tell her, past midnight. She says, "Good," about the parts that are, and nothing about the rest.}
opt.left.say.1 [b98630] = {你一直说到灯芯快灭，早过了睡觉的时辰。她听到那位扔粉笔的教授时哈哈大笑，说到决斗时却一下子安静了。|你讲你的朋友们，一直讲到灯灭。她对每个人都问了两个问题，问得都正是地方。|你一直讲到过了午夜。好的部分，她说一声“好”；其余的，她什么也没说。}
# en: Ask about the valley instead
opt.right.label [f0a37d] = 改问山谷里的事
# en: {She tells you about the old drovers' road and the chapel the marsh took. When you ask about the villages, she says they're very hospitable, in a voice that closes the subject.|She tells you who's married whom and who's buried where. She doesn't say why the inn's guest book is the one thing she won't let you fetch.|She talks about the marsh like a person: what it wants, what it gives back. Then she changes the subject, so carefully you notice.}
opt.right.say.1 [3d44c9] = {她给你讲了老赶牲口的路，还有被沼泽吞掉的那座礼拜堂。你问起那两个村子，她说他们非常好客，那语气把话题关上了。|她告诉你谁娶了谁、谁葬在哪儿。她没说为什么客栈的留客簿是她唯一不让你去拿的东西。|她说起沼泽就像说起一个人：它想要什么，它还回来什么。然后她换了话题，换得那么小心，让你注意到了。}

@event marsh_witch_stranger
# en: The Woman on the Stilt House Steps
title [65d791] = 高脚屋台阶上的女人
# en: {The hedge-witch is sitting on her steps with a bunch of rue in her lap, and doesn't look up when you pass. "Visiting," she says. It isn't a question.|The hedge-witch again. This time she looks at you, once, as if counting something. "Mind the inn," she says.|She's waiting on the steps as if she knew you'd come. "Still here," she says, and it sounds like a worry.} {season == "winter": Her breath smokes; she doesn't seem to feel the cold.|Dragonflies settle on the rail beside her.}
text [ba7e85] = {乡野女巫坐在自家台阶上，膝上放着一束芸香，你走过时她头也不抬。“来做客的，”她说。这不是在问你。|又是那位乡野女巫。这回她看了你一眼，只一眼，像在数什么。“当心那家客栈，”她说。|她在台阶上等着，好像早知道你会来。“还在这儿啊，”她说，听起来像是在担心。} {season == "winter": 她呼出的气冒着白烟；她好像不觉得冷。|蜻蜓落在她身旁的栏杆上。}
# en: An old woman sitting on the steps of a house on stilts at the edge of a marsh, a bunch of grey-green herbs in her lap, not looking at the student on the path.
scene [c8c8b6] = 沼泽边一座高脚屋的台阶上坐着一位老妇人，膝上放着一束灰绿色的草药，没有看小路上的学生。
# en: Ask what she means
opt.left.label [cb3024] = 问她什么意思
# en: {She ties a sprig of rue with a bit of red thread and holds it out. "A penny. Nothing's free." You pay. "Keep it in your pocket while you're in the valley, and don't let the inn wash your coat."|{flag(marsh_rue): She gives you another sprig, though you still have the first. "For whoever you're travelling with."|She ties you a sprig of rue with red thread. "For the road," she says.} She takes the penny and won't say more.|"You know what I mean," she says, which you don't, and takes your penny for {flag(marsh_rue): another sprig|a sprig of rue on red thread}.}
opt.left.say.1 [5f07ad] = {她用一截红线扎好一小枝芸香，递了过来。“一便士。没有白给的东西。”你付了钱。“待在山谷里的时候把它揣在兜里，别让客栈给你洗外套。”|{flag(marsh_rue): 她又给了你一枝，虽然你那一枝还在。“给跟你同行的人。”|她用红线给你扎了一小枝芸香。“路上带着，”她说。} 她收下便士，别的什么也不肯说了。|“你知道我是什么意思，”她说，可你并不知道。她收下你的便士，换给你{flag(marsh_rue): 又一枝|一枝扎着红线的芸香}。}
# en: Wish her good day and walk on
opt.right.label [a66777] = 道声日安，继续走
# en: {"Good day," she says to the marsh, not to you. Behind you, you hear her shutters close.|You wish her good day. She says, "Is it," and goes back to her herbs.|You walk on. When you look back she's standing, watching the road to the villages, not you.}
opt.right.say.1 [a8df23] = {“日安，”她对着沼泽说，不是对你。你身后传来她关上窗板的声音。|你祝她日安。她说“是吗”，又低头摆弄她的草药。|你继续往前走。回头看时，她站了起来，望着通往村子的路，而不是你。}

@event marsh_lights_on_the_drovers_road
# en: The Drovers' Road
title [2a8518] = 赶牲口的老路
# en: {At dusk the lights come out over the Marsh, and tonight they line up along the old drovers' road, the half-sunk causeway nobody uses, as if marking it for someone.|The lights are on the drovers' road again, and closer together, like a queue.|The lights are already on the causeway when you come, and one of them, you'd swear, is waiting at your end.} {season == "winter": The water between the stones has a skin of ice.|Frogs go silent as you step onto the stones.}
text [b64ffe] = {黄昏时沼泽上的光出来了，今晚它们沿着赶牲口的老路排成一行——那条半沉在水里、没人走的堤道——像是在给什么人标出路来。|光又排在那条老路上了，挨得更近，像在排队。|你来的时候光已经在堤道上了，你敢发誓，其中有一点正在你这头等着。} {season == "winter": 石块之间的水结了一层薄冰。|你一踏上石块，青蛙就不叫了。}
# en: A line of small pale lights strung along a half-sunken causeway across a marsh at dusk, a student standing at its end with a lantern.
scene [9baf5a] = 黄昏时，一串苍白的小光点沿着一条半沉在沼泽里的堤道排开，一个提着灯的学生站在堤道这头。
# en: Walk the causeway a little way
opt.left.label [5fe49b] = 在堤道上走一小段
# en: {You go six stones out. The lights keep their distance exactly, and the seventh stone is underwater. You come back wet to the knee and certain that the road went somewhere once.|You go further this time. Halfway, the lights move aside to let you pass, which is worse than if they'd blocked you. You turn back.|You walk out until the lights are all round you. None of them is warm. When you come back the hedge-witch's lamp is lit, and her shutters are open.}
opt.left.say.1 [ebf7d7] = {你往外走了六块石头。那些光始终保持着同样的距离，而第七块石头沉在水下。你湿到膝盖回来，确信这条路从前通往某个地方。|这回你走得更远。走到一半，光挪开让你过去，这比挡住你还糟。你掉头了。|你一直走到四周全是光。没有一点是暖的。回来时乡野女巫的灯亮着，窗板开着。}
# en: Watch from the bank
opt.right.label [6f8a23] = 在岸上看着
# en: {You watch them until full dark, and then they go out one by one, from the far end, like a house being shut up.|You watch from the bank. The lights stay, and so do you, until you realise you've been counting them.|You don't go out. One light comes as far as the bank, hangs there, and goes back. You walk home faster than you meant to.}
opt.right.say.1 [a820ea] = {你一直看到天全黑，然后它们从远端开始一个接一个熄灭，像一座房子被关门落锁。|你在岸上看着。光没走，你也没走，直到你发觉自己一直在数它们。|你没走出去。有一点光一直来到岸边，悬在那儿，又回去了。你走回去时比你想的要快。}

@event marsh_drowned_chapel
# en: The Chapel the Marsh Took
title [c83696] = 被沼泽吞掉的礼拜堂
# en: {The water's low today, and out in the reeds there's a roof, a little chapel's slate roof, and an empty bell turret, standing in the marsh up to its eaves.|The drowned chapel again, a hand's width more of it showing. Someone has tied a ribbon to the turret.|The chapel's door lintel is just above the water now. It has something carved on it, worn smooth.} {season == "winter": Ice rims the turret's arch.|Moorhens have nested in the turret.}
text [053463] = {今天水位低，芦苇丛里露出一个屋顶，一座小礼拜堂的石板屋顶和一座空钟塔，整座礼拜堂泡在沼泽里，水一直淹到屋檐。|又是那座淹没的礼拜堂，比上次多露出一掌宽。有人在钟塔上系了一根带子。|礼拜堂的门楣刚好露出水面。上面刻着什么，已经磨平了。} {season == "winter": 钟塔的拱圈结了一圈冰。|一对黑水鸡在钟塔里筑了巢。}
# en: The slate roof and empty bell turret of a small chapel showing above reeds and still water, a student on a tussock nearby with a sketchbook.
scene [6e8d96] = 芦苇和静水之上露出一座小礼拜堂的石板屋顶和空空的钟塔，一个学生拿着速写本站在近旁的草墩上。
# en: Wade out to it
opt.left.label [21bc1c] = 蹚水过去
# en: {Waist-deep, freezing, you reach the turret. No bell, and no fittings for one either; the turret was built empty. That seems a strange thing to build.|You reach the ribbon. It's red thread, knotted seven times, and new.|You get close enough to read the lintel: a sheaf of wheat, carved over and over in a band, and a date too worn to read.}
opt.left.say.1 [f8cb38] = {水齐腰深，冷得刺骨，你终于够到了钟楼。没有钟，连挂钟的架子都没有；这座钟楼本来就是空着建的。建这么个东西，真是奇怪。|你够到了那条丝带。是红线，打了七个结，还是新的。|你凑得够近，看清了门楣：一圈反复刻着的麦束，还有一个磨得认不出的年份。}
# en: {The bottom goes out from under you halfway. You come back soaked to the neck with nothing to show but a leech.|You go in up to your chest and decide the chapel can keep its secrets. The marsh keeps your left boot.|You slip on a submerged step and go under. When you come up, the turret is exactly as far away as before.}
opt.left.say.2 [3fe3b8] = {走到一半，脚下一空。你湿到脖子回来，除了一条水蛭什么也没捞着。|水没到胸口，你决定礼拜堂的秘密还是留给它自己吧。沼泽留下了你的左靴。|你在一级没在水下的台阶上滑倒，整个人沉了下去。等你冒出水面，钟塔还是和刚才一样远。}
# en: Sketch it from the bank
opt.right.label [66e4b9] = 在岸上画下来
# en: {You draw the roof and the turret. Later, looking at the sketch, you notice you've drawn a bell in the turret. There isn't one.|You sketch it again, from the same tussock. It's higher out of the water than last time; you draw the new course of stones.|You sketch the lintel through the reeds. The carving might be wheat. Most things carved round here seem to be.}
opt.right.say.1 [7ae65a] = {你画下屋顶和钟楼。后来再看这幅速写，你发现自己在钟楼里画了一口钟。可那里并没有钟。|你又在同一个草墩上画了一遍。它比上回露出水面更多了；你把新露出的那一层石头也画了进去。|你隔着芦苇画下门楣。那雕刻也许是麦子。这一带刻的东西，好像大多都是麦子。}

@event marsh_eel_catcher
# en: The Eel Traps
title [94bd9a] = 鳗鱼笼
# en: {An eel-catcher in waders is lifting his traps along the channel, and he talks to every one before he opens it.|The eel-catcher again, and the traps again, and the same small speech to each one. "Manners," he explains.|The eel-catcher knows your face by now, and waves you over with a trap. "You'll do the talking today."} {season == "winter": The channels are slow and black; the eels are sleepy.|The eels are lively and so are the midges.}
text [0d6a26] = {一个穿着涉水裤的捕鳗人正沿着水渠一个个提起鳗笼，每打开一个之前都要跟它说几句话。|又是那个捕鳗人，又是那些笼子，又是对每个笼子说的那几句小话。“礼数，”他解释道。|捕鳗人如今认得你了，提着一只笼子招手叫你过去。“今天你来说话。”} {season == "winter": 水渠流得又慢又黑；鳗鱼都昏昏欲睡。|鳗鱼很活泼，蠓虫也是。}
# en: A weathered fen-man in waders lifting a wicker eel trap out of a marsh channel, a student watching from a plank path with a parcel of smoked fish.
scene [871eeb] = 一个饱经风霜、穿着涉水裤的沼泽汉子从沼泽水道里提起一只柳条鳗鱼笼，一个学生拿着一包熏鱼站在木板路上看着。
# en: Help him with the traps
opt.left.label [f0b4db] = 帮他起笼
# en: {You haul six traps and get bitten by one eel. He pays you in smoked eel and a piece of advice. Never, he says, count the stones on the ridge out loud.|You talk to the traps, feeling a fool, wet and cold to the wrist. The catch is good. "See," he says.|You haul all morning, wet to the elbows. He tells you the marsh used to be a village, "before they stopped paying," then pretends he said "the drainage".}
opt.left.say.1 [13d1ef] = {你拖上来六只笼子，被一条鳗鱼咬了一口。他用熏鳗鱼和一句忠告付你工钱：千万别把山脊上的石头大声数出来。|你对着笼子说话，觉得自己像个傻瓜，手一直冻到手腕。收获不错。“看吧，”他说。|你拖了一上午，湿到手肘。他告诉你沼泽从前是个村子，“在他们不再付钱之前”，然后又假装自己说的是“排水之前”。}
# en: Buy some smoked eel
opt.right.label [6fcada] = 买些熏鳗鱼
# en: {Smoked eel in a twist of paper, eaten on the plank path. It's oily, smoky and better than anything in the refectory.|He wraps you a piece of the good stuff without being asked. "For the walk back," he says. "Don't take the drovers' road."|Smoked eel from the back of the smokehouse, the good stuff. He won't say why the inn doesn't buy from him.}
opt.right.say.1 [3e7c3c] = {一卷纸包着的熏鳗鱼，站在木板路上吃完。油润、带着烟熏味，比食堂里的任何东西都好吃。|他没等你开口，就给你包了一块上好的。“回去路上吃，”他说。“别走赶畜道。”|熏房最里头的熏鳗鱼，上等货。他不肯说为什么客栈不从他这儿买。}
